      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it exceeds the maximum acetaminophen dose.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg \u00d7 3 = 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual 1000 mg maximum per dose for a 70 kg adult.\n- **Risk:** Even with normal liver function, this dosing carries a significant risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n1. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3 g/day). This keeps the same TID schedule at a standard dose.\n2. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 g/day, max). Your institution's policy may set a lower cap.\n3. **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day), if you want a more conservative dose.\n\nIf you meant 2000 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it as 650 mg PO TID (1950 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO BID.\n\nIf you intend 2000 mg TID, please confirm explicitly with your clinical rationale. Pharmacy will likely need to verify it, and I'd want that documented.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter? Also, please tell me if the patient is on any other acetaminophen-containing products so I can account for them in the daily total."
     }
